From: ps5cemu <ps5cemu@localhost>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:38:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: the game camera projects for the aspect of the image the
 game renders

m_gameRenderAspectRatio was set from the image only in the Windows path (framebuffer.cpp); on Linux it stayed 16:9, so a render at the eye's shape (the Graphics pack, 1280x1320) got a 16:9 expanded projection squeezed into a nearly square image, and the crop (which takes the aspect from the image) did not undo it: a wrong field of view and eye offsets. A capture target the 3D path refuses (not the display format) does not set it.
---
 src/rendering/renderer_vulkan.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/rendering/renderer_vulkan.cpp b/src/rendering/renderer_vulkan.cpp
index 1b5ddc8..fdf0fde 100644
--- a/src/rendering/renderer_vulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/rendering/renderer_vulkan.cpp
@@ -1732,6 +1732,10 @@ void RND_Renderer::LinuxHandleColorClear(OpenXR::EyeSide side, long captureIdx,
         if (captureIdx == 0) {
             const bool is3DColorTarget = srcFormat == VK_FORMAT_A2B10G10R10_UNORM_PACK32;
             if (is3DColorTarget) {
+                // The game camera projects for this aspect (camera.cpp); only the Windows path took it
+                // from the image, so a Graphics pack that renders at the eye's shape was projected as
+                // 16:9. A refused target (the log line below) can have another size: it must not set it.
+                m_gameRenderAspectRatio = (float)srcWidth / (float)srcHeight;
                 hudCapturedThisFrame = false;
                 // Apply pause transitions only at a left-eye boundary. The menu state
                 // often flips between the left and right clears; resetting there strands
